nodecode-structured-aux is a rewrite of trajectoire-ai's trajectoire-ai/hermes-structured-aux-models:
https://github.com/trajectoire-ai/hermes-structured-aux-models
commit e5c49b081ad04adca2ee3edc601b09ede6cee4c5
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Trajectoire AI (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the decision transport (the one POST to /api/alpha/decisions, with
its bearer key and its app-attribution headers), the payload redaction applied
before anything leaves, the three contracts (approval, MCP tool choice,
extractive compression) with the labels, criteria and instructions the original
states, and the segmentation and digest assembly, including the rule that a
digest is never empty and that an unanswered block fails rather than being
guessed. Left out: the model-provider registration and its OpenAI-shaped
in-process client, because Nodecode has no auxiliary-task seam for a provider to
serve (the verbs are called from eval instead), the placeholder subprocess gate
that only existed to pass it, the Hermes credential pool read (the key comes
from auth.json under api_keys.openrouter, else OPENROUTER_API_KEY), and the
moving tasks list, which became four verbs.
